# Environment template for the International Fair card game.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and adjust it for your machine; `.env.local` is git-ignored.
#
# This project uses no API keys or secrets. The only setting is optional:
# leave it empty and the build auto-detects Chrome / Edge / Chromium.
# Precedence: shell environment > .env.local > .env > config/print-settings.json (browser.executable_path).

# Full path to a Chromium-based browser used (headless) to render the PDFs and the prototype image.
# Examples:
#   Windows (Chrome): C:/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe
#   Windows (Edge):   C:/Program Files (x86)/Microsoft/Edge/Application/msedge.exe
#   macOS (Chrome):   /Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome
#   Linux:            /usr/bin/chromium
CHROME_PATH=
